#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""claude-usage-report -- where Claude Code's tokens went: by project, day, model and subagent.

WHY IT EXISTS. Several long-lived Claude Code sessions, plus the subagents they spawn, can share
one flat-rate subscription with a weekly usage limit. When the limit runs out early, the first
question is where the tokens went and whether that was efficient: which project, which day, the
main session or its subagents, which model, how many subagents. Claude Code's own transcripts hold
that data. This tool reads them and prints counts. It never prints transcript content: no prompts,
no message text, no file contents, no subagent descriptions. It only reads; it writes nothing.

    claude-usage-report [--days N | --since YYYY-MM-DD] [--until YYYY-MM-DD] [--json]
    claude-usage-report --sessions [--seat PATTERN]... [window flags] [--json]

The window is the last 7 days by default, judged by each record's own timestamp. `--since` starts
at local midnight of that date; `--until` ends at the close of that local date. `--json` prints the
same report as one JSON object.

PER-SESSION VIEW (--sessions). One row per main-session transcript, for judging when a long-lived
session should be refreshed. A session is listed when any of its requests falls in the window, and
its row covers the whole session, so the context columns are not cut off at the window's edge.
`--seat` keeps sessions whose seat name matches the shell-style pattern (`--seat 'mod-*'`); give it
more than once for several. The columns:

    seat         the session's name: its custom title (what the agents view shows), else its
                 agent name, else "-".
    session      the first 8 characters of the session id (the transcript's file name).
    start, end   local time of the session's first and last request.
    reqs         requests: API calls, counted once per unique message.id (see DOUBLE COUNTING).
    ctx@1, ctx@10, ctx@50, ctx@end
                 the context sent with request 1, 10, 50 and the last one: that request's input +
                 cache-read + cache-write tokens, which is the whole prompt the model was given.
                 ctx@1 is the session's fixed startup cost (system prompt, always-on context, the
                 first message); the climb from there is the conversation accumulating. "-" when
                 the session made fewer requests than that.
    avg ctx      total input divided by reqs: the average prompt size.
    total input  the sum over every request of input + cache-read + cache-write. This is the usage
                 proxy, because every request re-sends the whole conversation, so the cost of a
                 session grows with context size times request count, and this sum is exactly that
                 product. Cache-read tokens are cheaper per token than fresh input, which this sum
                 does not weigh (see BLIND SPOTS); it measures how much context was carried.
    cache write  tokens written to the prompt cache, summed: new context, plus any context the
                 cache had dropped and had to rebuild (a long pause between requests does this).
    output       tokens the model generated, summed.
    sub input    total input of the session's subagents, which run in their own contexts and are
                 not part of any ctx column.
    cmp          compactions: how many times the context was summarized and cut.
    ended        how the session finished:
                   parked     it ran `fleet-canonicals stage` (it wrote and staged a handoff).
                   live       its process is still running.
                   compacted  not parked and not running, and it compacted at least once.
                   exited     not parked, not running, never compacted.
                   open       not parked, and whether it is running cannot be seen from here:
                              inside a sandbox with its own process namespace, other sessions'
                              processes are invisible. Run it from a plain terminal to resolve.

The live check reads Claude Code's session records ($CLAUDE_SESSIONS_DIR, default
~/.claude/sessions): a record naming the session id whose process exists, and was started at the
recorded time, so a reused process id does not count. Records only cover sessions on this machine.

A session that was resumed or forked carries the earlier messages in its own transcript, so its
row includes them, and summing rows across such sessions counts them twice.

DATA SOURCE. Transcripts under $CLAUDE_PROJECTS_DIR (default ~/.claude/projects):

    <project-key>/<session-id>.jsonl                          the main session
    <project-key>/<session-id>/subagents/agent-<id>.jsonl     one subagent
    <project-key>/<session-id>/subagents/agent-<id>.meta.json its agent type (`agentType`)

Each line is one JSON record. Records of type "assistant" carry message.id, message.model and
message.usage (input_tokens, output_tokens, cache_creation_input_tokens, cache_read_input_tokens).
Files are streamed line by line, since a transcript can be hundreds of megabytes. A line that is
not JSON, or a record without usage, is skipped. A "<synthetic>" model with zero usage is skipped.

DOUBLE COUNTING. A streamed message is written as several records with the same message.id, and
the usage in them is cumulative within the stream. Summing them overcounts badly (one session had
469 usage records for 221 messages). Records are therefore merged by message.id, keeping each usage
field's MAXIMUM, and a message is dated by its earliest record.

PROJECT. A record's `cwd` reduced to its repository root: a trailing `/.worktrees/<name>` and
anything below it is stripped, then, if the directory still exists, the nearest ancestor holding a
`.git` entry is used (sessions often run in a subdirectory). $HOME is shown as `~`. Without a cwd,
the project-key directory name is used.

READING THE NUMBERS. Cache-read tokens dwarf everything else, and that is expected. Every turn
re-sends the whole conversation as context, and the part already cached is billed as a cache read,
so a long session re-reads its history on each turn. The cache-read count therefore grows with
session length times turn count; it says how much context was carried, not how much was written.
Output tokens are the model's generated text and cost far more per token.

BLIND SPOTS.
  - The transcripts give no price weights, and the plan's limit is not published in tokens, so
    tokens cannot be converted into percent of the limit. The optional limit history (below) is
    the only direct measure of the limit itself.
  - Token kinds are counted, not weighed: a cache-read token and an output token count as one each.
  - Only what survives on disk is seen. Deleted transcripts, and activity from other machines or
    other accounts, are absent. A message appearing in several files is counted once.
  - A subagent whose meta.json is missing has type "unknown".
  - Day boundaries are the machine's local time.

LIMIT HISTORY. If $CLAUDE_USAGE_HISTORY (default ~/.local/state/claude-usage/history.jsonl)
exists, each line {"ts": epoch seconds, "five_hour_pct", "seven_day_pct", ...} is folded into a
per-day table: first and last seven_day_pct (their difference is how much of the weekly limit that
day used) and the maximum five_hour_pct. When the file is absent the report says so in one line.

Test hooks: CLAUDE_USAGE_NOW (epoch seconds) replaces the clock; CLAUDE_USAGE_PID_NS replaces this
process's pid namespace (the `pid:[N]` link) for the live check. Python 3 stdlib only.
"""
import argparse
import calendar
import fnmatch
import json
import os
import sys
import time
from datetime import datetime, timezone

KINDS = ("messages", "output", "cache_creation", "cache_read", "input")
USAGE_FIELDS = (("output_tokens", "output"), ("cache_creation_input_tokens", "cache_creation"),
                ("cache_read_input_tokens", "cache_read"), ("input_tokens", "input"))


def now_epoch():
    v = os.environ.get("CLAUDE_USAGE_NOW")
    return float(v) if v else time.time()


def parse_ts(s):
    """ISO 8601 (with Z or offset) to epoch seconds, or None."""
    if not isinstance(s, str):
        return None
    try:
        return datetime.fromisoformat(s.replace("Z", "+00:00")).timestamp()
    except ValueError:
        return None


_ROOTS = {}


def repo_root(path):
    """The nearest ancestor of path (itself included) holding a .git entry, else path."""
    if path in _ROOTS:
        return _ROOTS[path]
    cur = path
    while cur and cur != os.path.dirname(cur):
        if os.path.exists(os.path.join(cur, ".git")):
            break
        cur = os.path.dirname(cur)
    else:
        cur = path
    _ROOTS[path] = cur
    return cur


def project_of(cwd, key, home):
    if not isinstance(cwd, str) or not cwd:
        return key
    i = cwd.find("/.worktrees/")
    if i >= 0:
        cwd = cwd[:i]
    elif cwd.endswith("/.worktrees"):
        cwd = cwd[: -len("/.worktrees")]
    cwd = repo_root(cwd)
    if home and (cwd == home or cwd.startswith(home + "/")):
        cwd = "~" + cwd[len(home):]
    return cwd


def read_messages(root, cutoff, home):
    """Merge assistant records by message.id. Returns a list of per-message dicts."""
    msgs = {}
    anon = 0
    try:
        keys = sorted(os.listdir(root))
    except OSError:
        return []
    for key in keys:
        kdir = os.path.join(root, key)
        if not os.path.isdir(kdir):
            continue
        for path, session, agent in transcript_files(kdir):
            try:
                if os.path.getmtime(path) < cutoff:
                    continue  # nothing in it can be newer than the file
                fh = open(path, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace")
            except OSError:
                continue
            with fh:
                for line in fh:
                    try:
                        r = json.loads(line)
                    except ValueError:
                        continue
                    if not isinstance(r, dict) or r.get("type") != "assistant":
                        continue
                    m = r.get("message")
                    if not isinstance(m, dict) or not isinstance(m.get("usage"), dict):
                        continue
                    u = m["usage"]
                    vals = {}
                    for src, dst in USAGE_FIELDS:
                        v = u.get(src)
                        vals[dst] = v if isinstance(v, int) and v > 0 else 0
                    model = m.get("model") if isinstance(m.get("model"), str) else "unknown"
                    if model == "<synthetic>" or not any(vals.values()):
                        continue
                    ts = parse_ts(r.get("timestamp"))
                    if ts is None:
                        continue
                    mid = m.get("id")
                    if not isinstance(mid, str) or not mid:
                        anon += 1
                        mid = "\0anon%d" % anon
                    cur = msgs.get(mid)
                    if cur is None:
                        side = bool(agent) or r.get("isSidechain") is True
                        aid = agent or (r.get("agentId") if isinstance(r.get("agentId"), str) else "")
                        msgs[mid] = cur = {
                            "ts": ts, "iso": r.get("timestamp"), "model": model, "side": side,
                            "agent": aid if side else "", "session": session or r.get("sessionId") or "?",
                            "project": project_of(r.get("cwd"), key, home), "key": key, **vals}
                    else:
                        for k, v in vals.items():
                            cur[k] = max(cur[k], v)
                        if ts < cur["ts"]:
                            cur["ts"], cur["iso"] = ts, r.get("timestamp")
    return [m for m in msgs.values() if m["ts"] >= cutoff]


def transcript_files(kdir):
    """Yield (path, session id, agent id or '') for a project-key directory."""
    for name in sorted(os.listdir(kdir)):
        p = os.path.join(kdir, name)
        if name.endswith(".jsonl") and os.path.isfile(p):
            yield p, name[:-6], ""
        elif os.path.isdir(p):
            sub = os.path.join(p, "subagents")
            if os.path.isdir(sub):
                for f in sorted(os.listdir(sub)):
                    if f.startswith("agent-") and f.endswith(".jsonl"):
                        yield os.path.join(sub, f), name, f[len("agent-"):-6]


def agent_type(root, msg):
    p = os.path.join(root, msg["key"], msg["session"], "subagents", "agent-%s.meta.json" % msg["agent"])
    try:
        with open(p, encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            t = json.load(fh).get("agentType")
        return t if isinstance(t, str) and t else "unknown"
    except (OSError, ValueError, AttributeError):
        return "unknown"


def zero():
    return {k: 0 for k in KINDS}


def add(tot, m):
    tot["messages"] += 1
    for k in KINDS[1:]:
        tot[k] += m[k]


def day_of(ts):
    return time.strftime("%Y-%m-%d", time.localtime(ts))


def build(root, cutoff, home, end=float("inf")):
    msgs = [m for m in read_messages(root, cutoff, home) if m["ts"] < end]
    projects, days, sessions = {}, {}, {}
    by_type, by_model, agents = {}, {}, {}
    for m in msgs:
        side = "subagent" if m["side"] else "main"
        p = projects.setdefault(m["project"], {"main": zero(), "subagent": zero(),
                                               "agents": set(), "models": {}})
        add(p[side], m)
        p["models"][m["model"]] = p["models"].get(m["model"], 0) + 1
        d = days.setdefault(day_of(m["ts"]), {"main": zero(), "subagent": zero()})
        add(d[side], m)
        s = sessions.setdefault((m["key"], m["session"]), {
            "session": m["session"], "project": m["project"], "models": {}, "agents": set(),
            "first": m["ts"], "last": m["ts"], "first_iso": m["iso"], "last_iso": m["iso"],
            "output": 0, "cache_read": 0})
        s["output"] += m["output"]
        s["cache_read"] += m["cache_read"]
        s["models"][m["model"]] = s["models"].get(m["model"], 0) + 1
        if m["ts"] < s["first"]:
            s["first"], s["first_iso"] = m["ts"], m["iso"]
        if m["ts"] > s["last"]:
            s["last"], s["last_iso"] = m["ts"], m["iso"]
        if m["side"]:
            aid = m["agent"] or "?"
            p["agents"].add((m["key"], m["session"], aid))
            s["agents"].add(aid)
            a = agents.setdefault((m["key"], m["session"], aid), {"type": agent_type(root, m), "models": {}})
            a["models"][m["model"]] = 1
            t = by_type.setdefault(a["type"], {"agents": set(), **zero()})
            t["agents"].add((m["key"], m["session"], aid))
            add(t, m)
            g = by_model.setdefault(m["model"], {"agents": set(), **zero()})
            g["agents"].add((m["key"], m["session"], aid))
            add(g, m)

    def groups(src):
        return {k: {"count": len(v["agents"]), **{x: v[x] for x in KINDS}} for k, v in sorted(src.items())}

    top = sorted(sessions.values(), key=lambda s: (-(s["cache_read"] + s["output"]), s["session"]))[:10]
    return {
        "projects": {k: {"main": v["main"], "subagent": v["subagent"], "subagents_spawned": len(v["agents"]),
                         "models": dict(sorted(v["models"].items()))} for k, v in sorted(projects.items())},
        "days": dict(sorted(days.items())),
        "subagents": {"by_type": groups(by_type), "by_model": groups(by_model)},
        "sessions": [{"session": s["session"], "project": s["project"],
                      "cache_read_plus_output": s["cache_read"] + s["output"],
                      "models": dict(sorted(s["models"].items())), "subagents": len(s["agents"]),
                      "first": s["first_iso"], "last": s["last_iso"]} for s in top],
    }


PARK_MARK = "fleet-canonicals stage "


def usage_vals(m):
    """The four usage counts of an assistant message, or None when it carries no real usage."""
    if not isinstance(m, dict) or not isinstance(m.get("usage"), dict):
        return None
    u = m["usage"]
    vals = {}
    for src, dst in USAGE_FIELDS:
        v = u.get(src)
        vals[dst] = v if isinstance(v, int) and v > 0 else 0
    if m.get("model") == "<synthetic>" or not any(vals.values()):
        return None
    return vals


def ran_park(m):
    """Whether an assistant message holds a Bash tool call that stages a handoff."""
    for c in m.get("content") or ():
        if isinstance(c, dict) and c.get("type") == "tool_use" and c.get("name") == "Bash":
            cmd = (c.get("input") or {}).get("command")
            if isinstance(cmd, str) and PARK_MARK in cmd:
                return True
    return False


def read_requests(path, main):
    """One transcript's requests in order, merged by message.id (each field's maximum).

    With main=True, sidechain records (subagent turns written into the main file by older Claude
    Code builds) are left out, and the seat name, compactions and park are collected too."""
    reqs, anon = {}, 0
    info = {"title": None, "agent_name": None, "compactions": 0, "parked": False, "cwd": None}
    try:
        fh = open(path, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace")
    except OSError:
        return [], info
    with fh:
        for line in fh:
            try:
                r = json.loads(line)
            except ValueError:
                continue
            if not isinstance(r, dict):
                continue
            t = r.get("type")
            if info["cwd"] is None and isinstance(r.get("cwd"), str):
                info["cwd"] = r["cwd"]
            if main and t == "custom-title" and isinstance(r.get("customTitle"), str):
                info["title"] = r["customTitle"]
            elif main and t == "agent-name" and isinstance(r.get("agentName"), str):
                info["agent_name"] = r["agentName"]
            elif main and t == "system" and r.get("subtype") == "compact_boundary":
                info["compactions"] += 1
            if t != "assistant" or (main and r.get("isSidechain") is True):
                continue
            m = r.get("message")
            if main and isinstance(m, dict) and not info["parked"] and ran_park(m):
                info["parked"] = True
            vals = usage_vals(m)
            ts = parse_ts(r.get("timestamp"))
            if vals is None or ts is None:
                continue
            mid = m.get("id")
            if not isinstance(mid, str) or not mid:
                anon += 1
                mid = "\0anon%d" % anon
            cur = reqs.get(mid)
            if cur is None:
                reqs[mid] = dict(ts=ts, **vals)
            else:
                for k, v in vals.items():
                    cur[k] = max(cur[k], v)
                cur["ts"] = min(cur["ts"], ts)
    return sorted(reqs.values(), key=lambda q: q["ts"]), info


def ctx(q):
    return q["input"] + q["cache_read"] + q["cache_creation"]


def own_pid_ns():
    v = os.environ.get("CLAUDE_USAGE_PID_NS")
    if v:
        return v
    try:
        return os.readlink("/proc/self/ns/pid")
    except OSError:
        return None  # no /proc (macOS): process ids are machine-wide, so a check is decisive


def proc_alive(pid, start):
    try:
        os.kill(pid, 0)
    except ProcessLookupError:
        return False
    except PermissionError:
        pass  # exists, owned by someone else
    except OSError:
        return False
    if start:
        try:
            with open("/proc/%d/stat" % pid) as fh:
                # field 22 is the start time; the name in field 2 may hold spaces, so split after ")"
                return fh.read().rsplit(")", 1)[1].split()[19] == str(start)
        except (OSError, IndexError):
            pass
    return True


def liveness(sessions_dir):
    """Map session id -> True (running), False (record but not running) or None (cannot see)."""
    out, ns = {}, own_pid_ns()
    try:
        names = os.listdir(sessions_dir)
    except OSError:
        return out
    for n in names:
        if not n.endswith(".json"):
            continue
        try:
            with open(os.path.join(sessions_dir, n), encoding="utf-8") as fh:
                d = json.load(fh)
            sid, pid = d["sessionId"], int(d["pid"])
        except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError, TypeError, AttributeError):
            continue
        dom = d.get("pidDomain")
        if ns and isinstance(dom, str) and dom.startswith("linux:") and not dom.endswith(":" + ns):
            state = None  # recorded in another pid namespace: invisible from here
        else:
            state = proc_alive(pid, d.get("procStart"))
        prev = out.get(sid, False)
        out[sid] = True if (state or prev) else (None if (state is None or prev is None) else False)
    return out


def build_sessions(root, cutoff, end, home, seats, sessions_dir):
    alive = liveness(sessions_dir)
    rows = []
    try:
        keys = sorted(os.listdir(root))
    except OSError:
        return rows
    for key in keys:
        kdir = os.path.join(root, key)
        if not os.path.isdir(kdir):
            continue
        for name in sorted(os.listdir(kdir)):
            path = os.path.join(kdir, name)
            if not name.endswith(".jsonl") or not os.path.isfile(path):
                continue
            try:
                if os.path.getmtime(path) < cutoff:
                    continue
            except OSError:
                continue
            reqs, info = read_requests(path, True)
            if not reqs or reqs[-1]["ts"] < cutoff or reqs[0]["ts"] >= end:
                continue
            seat = info["title"] or info["agent_name"] or "-"
            if seats and not any(fnmatch.fnmatchcase(seat, p) for p in seats):
                continue
            sid = name[:-6]
            sub_reqs, sub_input = 0, 0
            sub = os.path.join(kdir, sid, "subagents")
            if os.path.isdir(sub):
                for f in sorted(os.listdir(sub)):
                    if f.startswith("agent-") and f.endswith(".jsonl"):
                        sr, _ = read_requests(os.path.join(sub, f), False)
                        sub_reqs += len(sr)
                        sub_input += sum(ctx(q) for q in sr)
            total = sum(ctx(q) for q in reqs)
            live = alive.get(sid, False)
            if info["parked"]:
                ended = "parked"
            elif live:
                ended = "live"
            elif live is None:
                ended = "open"
            else:
                ended = "compacted" if info["compactions"] else "exited"
            rows.append({
                "seat": seat, "session": sid, "project": project_of(info["cwd"], key, home),
                "start": reqs[0]["ts"], "end": reqs[-1]["ts"], "requests": len(reqs),
                "context": {"first": ctx(reqs[0]),
                            "at_10": ctx(reqs[9]) if len(reqs) >= 10 else None,
                            "at_50": ctx(reqs[49]) if len(reqs) >= 50 else None,
                            "last": ctx(reqs[-1])},
                "avg_context": round(total / len(reqs)),
                "total_input": total,
                "input": sum(q["input"] for q in reqs),
                "cache_read": sum(q["cache_read"] for q in reqs),
                "cache_write": sum(q["cache_creation"] for q in reqs),
                "output": sum(q["output"] for q in reqs),
                "subagent_requests": sub_reqs, "subagent_total_input": sub_input,
                "compactions": info["compactions"], "ended": ended})
    rows.sort(key=lambda s: (s["start"], s["session"]))
    return rows


def short(n):
    if n is None:
        return "-"
    if n >= 1e9:
        return "%.2fB" % (n / 1e9)
    if n >= 1e6:
        return "%.2fM" % (n / 1e6)
    if n >= 1e3:
        return "%.0fk" % (n / 1e3)
    return str(n)


def human_sessions(rows, window):
    o = ["claude-usage-report --sessions: " + window, "",
         "One row per session. ctx@N is the prompt sent with request N (input + cache-read +",
         "cache-write); total input sums it over every request and is the usage proxy, because each",
         "request re-sends the whole conversation. `claude-usage-report --help` defines every column.", ""]
    head = ["seat", "session", "start", "end", "reqs", "ctx@1", "ctx@10", "ctx@50", "ctx@end",
            "avg ctx", "total input", "cache write", "output", "sub input", "cmp", "ended"]
    hm = lambda ts: time.strftime("%m-%d %H:%M", time.localtime(ts))
    body = [[s["seat"], s["session"][:8], hm(s["start"]), hm(s["end"]), s["requests"],
             short(s["context"]["first"]), short(s["context"]["at_10"]), short(s["context"]["at_50"]),
             short(s["context"]["last"]), short(s["avg_context"]), short(s["total_input"]),
             short(s["cache_write"]), short(s["output"]), short(s["subagent_total_input"]),
             s["compactions"], s["ended"]] for s in rows]
    if not body:
        return "\n".join(o + ["No sessions in the window."])
    return "\n".join(o + table(head, body))


def read_history(path, cutoff, end=float("inf")):
    """Per-day limit usage from the history file, or None when it does not exist."""
    try:
        fh = open(path, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace")
    except OSError:
        return None
    rows = []
    with fh:
        for line in fh:
            try:
                r = json.loads(line)
                ts = float(r["ts"])
            except (ValueError, KeyError, TypeError):
                continue
            if isinstance(r, dict) and cutoff <= ts < end:
                rows.append((ts, r))
    rows.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])
    out = {}
    for ts, r in rows:
        d = out.setdefault(day_of(ts), {})
        seven, five = r.get("seven_day_pct"), r.get("five_hour_pct")
        if isinstance(seven, (int, float)):
            d.setdefault("seven_day_first", seven)
            d["seven_day_last"] = seven
        if isinstance(five, (int, float)):
            d["five_hour_max"] = max(d.get("five_hour_max", five), five)
    for d in out.values():
        if "seven_day_first" in d:
            d["seven_day_delta"] = round(d["seven_day_last"] - d["seven_day_first"], 2)
    return out


def fmt(n):
    if n >= 1e9:
        return "%.2fB" % (n / 1e9)
    if n >= 1e6:
        return "%.2fM" % (n / 1e6)
    return "{:,}".format(n)


def mix(models):
    return ", ".join("%s x%d" % kv for kv in sorted(models.items(), key=lambda kv: (-kv[1], kv[0])))


def table(head, rows):
    rows = [[("..." + str(c)[-57:]) if j == 0 and len(str(c)) > 60 else c for j, c in enumerate(r)] for r in rows]
    cols = list(zip(*([head] + rows)))
    w = [max(len(str(c)) for c in col) for col in cols]
    lines = []
    for i, r in enumerate([head] + rows):
        lines.append("  " + "  ".join(str(c).ljust(w[0]) if j == 0 else str(c).rjust(w[j])
                                      for j, c in enumerate(r)).rstrip())
        if i == 0:
            lines.append("  " + "  ".join("-" * x for x in w))
    return lines


def human(rep, window):
    o = ["claude-usage-report: " + window, "",
         "Cache-read dominates by design: every turn re-sends the whole conversation, and the",
         "cached part is billed as a cache read, so long sessions re-read their history each turn.",
         "Output tokens are the generated text. Blind spot: transcripts carry no price weights, so",
         "tokens cannot be converted into percent of the weekly limit; compare, do not convert.", ""]
    head = ["project", "msgs", "output", "cache-new", "cache-read", "input", "agents", "sub msgs", "sub out", "sub cache-read"]
    rows = []
    for k, v in rep["projects"].items():
        m, s = v["main"], v["subagent"]
        rows.append([k, fmt(m["messages"]), fmt(m["output"]), fmt(m["cache_creation"]), fmt(m["cache_read"]),
                     fmt(m["input"]), v["subagents_spawned"], fmt(s["messages"]), fmt(s["output"]), fmt(s["cache_read"])])
    o += ["By project (main session; sub = subagents)"] + table(head, rows)
    o += [""] + ["  models: %s -> %s" % (k, mix(v["models"])) for k, v in rep["projects"].items()] + [""]
    head = ["day", "msgs", "output", "cache-read", "sub msgs", "sub out", "sub cache-read"]
    rows = [[k, fmt(v["main"]["messages"]), fmt(v["main"]["output"]), fmt(v["main"]["cache_read"]),
             fmt(v["subagent"]["messages"]), fmt(v["subagent"]["output"]), fmt(v["subagent"]["cache_read"])]
            for k, v in rep["days"].items()]
    o += ["By day (local time)"] + table(head, rows) + [""]
    head = ["group", "agents", "msgs", "output", "cache-read"]
    for label, src in (("type", rep["subagents"]["by_type"]), ("model", rep["subagents"]["by_model"])):
        rows = [[k, v["count"], fmt(v["messages"]), fmt(v["output"]), fmt(v["cache_read"])] for k, v in src.items()]
        o += ["Subagents by " + label] + table([label] + head[1:], rows) + [""]
    head = ["session", "project", "cache-read+out", "subagents", "first", "last", "models"]
    rows = [[s["session"][:8], s["project"], fmt(s["cache_read_plus_output"]), s["subagents"],
             s["first"], s["last"], mix(s["models"])] for s in rep["sessions"]]
    o += ["Top sessions by cache-read + output"] + table(head, rows) + [""]
    lim = rep["limits"]
    if lim is None:
        o.append("Weekly limit: no usage history file found, so limit use per day is not shown.")
    else:
        head = ["day", "7d first %", "7d last %", "7d delta", "5h max %"]
        rows = [[k, v.get("seven_day_first", "-"), v.get("seven_day_last", "-"), v.get("seven_day_delta", "-"),
                 v.get("five_hour_max", "-")] for k, v in lim.items()]
        o += ["Weekly limit use per day (from the usage history)"] + table(head, rows)
    return "\n".join(o)


def local_midnight(ap, flag, v):
    try:
        return time.mktime(time.strptime(v, "%Y-%m-%d"))
    except ValueError:
        ap.error("%s wants YYYY-MM-DD" % flag)


def main(argv):
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="claude-usage-report", description=__doc__,
                                 formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
    g = ap.add_mutually_exclusive_group()
    g.add_argument("--days", type=int, help="window: the last N days (default 7)")
    g.add_argument("--since", help="window: from local midnight of YYYY-MM-DD")
    ap.add_argument("--until", help="window: through the end of local date YYYY-MM-DD")
    ap.add_argument("--sessions", action="store_true", help="one row per session (see PER-SESSION VIEW)")
    ap.add_argument("--seat", action="append", default=[], metavar="PATTERN",
                    help="with --sessions: only seats matching this shell-style pattern; repeatable")
    ap.add_argument("--json", action="store_true", help="emit one JSON object")
    a = ap.parse_args(argv)
    if a.seat and not a.sessions:
        ap.error("--seat needs --sessions")
    now = now_epoch()
    if a.since:
        cutoff = local_midnight(ap, "--since", a.since)
        window = "since %s" % a.since
    else:
        days = 7 if a.days is None else a.days
        if days < 0:
            ap.error("--days must not be negative")
        cutoff = now - days * 86400
        window = "last %d days" % days
    end = float("inf")
    if a.until:
        # the next local midnight; mktime normalizes day 32 and the like, and handles DST
        local_midnight(ap, "--until", a.until)  # refuses a malformed date
        t = time.strptime(a.until, "%Y-%m-%d")
        end = time.mktime((t.tm_year, t.tm_mon, t.tm_mday + 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, -1))
        window += " until %s" % a.until
    home = os.path.expanduser("~")
    root = os.environ.get("CLAUDE_PROJECTS_DIR") or os.path.join(home, ".claude", "projects")
    if a.sessions:
        sdir = os.environ.get("CLAUDE_SESSIONS_DIR") or os.path.join(home, ".claude", "sessions")
        rows = build_sessions(root, cutoff, end, home, a.seat, sdir)
        if a.json:
            for r in rows:
                r["start"] = datetime.fromtimestamp(r["start"], timezone.utc).isoformat()
                r["end"] = datetime.fromtimestamp(r["end"], timezone.utc).isoformat()
            print(json.dumps({"window": {"description": window, "from_epoch": int(cutoff),
                                         "to_epoch": int(min(end, now))}, "sessions": rows}, indent=1))
        else:
            print(human_sessions(rows, window))
        return 0
    hist = os.environ.get("CLAUDE_USAGE_HISTORY") or os.path.join(home, ".local", "state", "claude-usage", "history.jsonl")
    rep = build(root, cutoff, home, end)
    rep["window"] = {"description": window, "from_epoch": int(cutoff), "to_epoch": int(min(end, now))}
    rep["limits"] = read_history(hist, cutoff, end)
    print(json.dumps(rep, indent=1) if a.json else human(rep, window))
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    try:
        sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
    except BrokenPipeError:
        sys.exit(0)
